the C33: riscv32's generic bindings

The Seiko Epson C33 (the WikiReader's CPU) runs no-MMU Linux with the
generic UAPI and syscall table that riscv32 has, so it takes riscv32's
generated modules.  Their structs carry no padding that depends on
riscv32's 8-byte u64 alignment (the C33 aligns u64 to 4; rustc lays
the structs out for the target).  The register-context structs
(ptrace's user_regs_struct, the signal context) are riscv32's and do
not describe the C33.

